.SH NAME
anpu-query - Filter findings across saved scan reports


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu query [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Filter findings from saved JSON scan reports (files, not the
SQLite history database — use \fBanpu show\fR for stored scans).

.PP
Examples:
  anpu query --severity high
  anpu query --dir ./my-reports --text xss
  anpu query --input ./reports/scan.json --text xss --json
  anpu query --category vulnerability --confidence confirmed --limit 20


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--category\fP=""
	finding category substring match

.PP
\fB--confidence\fP=""
	minimum confidence: low, medium, high, confirmed

.PP
\fB--dir\fP="./reports"
	directory to auto-pick newest reports from (matches scan --output)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for query

.PP
\fB--input\fP=[]
	report JSON to query (repeatable; default: newest in --dir)

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print matches as JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	max findings to print (0 = all)

.PP
\fB--severity\fP=""
	minimum severity floor: low, medium, high, critical

.PP
\fB--text\fP=""
	case-insensitive substring over id/title/description/url


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu(1)\fP


